            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nI can reproduce. This is not really a 'mini.completion' issue, but a LuaLS plus its setup. Using `vim.api.nvim_get_runtime_file(\"\", true)` as part of the `library` seems to make LuaLS struggle to quickly initialize its scope. After LuaLS is done with initial loading, everything seems to work relatively smoothly.\n\nClosing as \"doesn't look like 'mini.completion' issue\".",
